        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define current-period quantities and prices, plus base-period prices\n    sugar_quantity = 120\n    sugar_december_price = 1.00\n    sugar_november_price = 0.90\n\n    cotton_quantity = 50\n    cotton_december_price = 0.80\n    cotton_november_price = 0.60\n\n    # Calculate the Paasche price index using December quantities\n    december_cost = (\n        sugar_quantity * sugar_december_price\n        + cotton_quantity * cotton_december_price\n    )\n    november_prices_cost = (\n        sugar_quantity * sugar_november_price\n        + cotton_quantity * cotton_november_price\n    )\n    answer = round(december_cost / november_prices_cost * 100, 3)\n\n    return answer\n```",
